The drop macro is a macro again

Run 569 did not compile.  The macro that records why a candidate was turned
away had lost the continuation backslashes from the lines this series added
to it, so the macro ended in the middle of the block and the rest of it
became code at the place where the macro is used:

  IOService.cpp:9739:48: error: expected 'while' in do/while loop

Every line of the macro is written out again here, with the continuations
where they belong.  The behaviour is the one that was meant: the reason and
the class of the personality that was turned away, the class of the first
one as well, and the mark on the panel.

